# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Python bytecode, written next to any script that gets imported (the world
# generators in simulationstudio/worlds/ import each other).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor directories and files
#
# `.vscode/*` has a slash in the middle, so it is anchored TO THE ROOT: it does
# NOT affect templates/project/.vscode/, which is template content and has to
# be published. The same goes for its .wpilib/, which is what makes the
# generated folder a robot project for the WPILib extension.
#
# extensions.json is kept on purpose: it holds the two recommended extensions
# (Tauri and rust-analyzer) for whoever clones this.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Working notes of Claude Code's design skill. A local tool, not project
# documentation.
.tastemaker/
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# --- desktop/ : MARS Desktop -----------------------------------------------
# `node_modules` and `dist` are already covered above (no slash, so they apply
# at any depth), and the Rust side is handled by desktop/src-tauri/.gitignore,
# which moved in with the folder.

# --- simulationstudio/ : MARS Simulation Studio -----------------------------
# build/ also holds the logs of the processes the Studio launches
# (app-*.log, app-*.err).
simulationstudio/build/
simulationstudio/install/
simulationstudio/dist/
simulationstudio/.gzsource/src/
# State persisted by nt-probe's NT4 server while the tests run.
simulationstudio/networktables.json

# Simulation bridge and Studio
simulationstudio/bridge/target/
simulationstudio/app/target/

# The Studio's 3D fields: 17 MB per field of third-party assets, and the Field
# Library reinstalls them in one click from the ones mars-desktop already has.
# A world that references a missing field still runs --- it loses the visuals,
# not the physics --- so ignoring them degrades gracefully.
simulationstudio/fields/

# --- installer/ -------------------------------------------------------------
installer/target/
installer/gen/schemas/

# --- lib/ : the MARS library ------------------------------------------------
# lib/.gitignore covers the gradle side (build/, .gradle/, the generated
# constants). What is NOT ignored, deliberately, is lib/maven/: the published
# jars live in the repository because they are what Pages serves to teams.

# --- docs/ + the Pages site -------------------------------------------------
docs/site/
docs/.cache/
# What .github/workflows/pages.yml assembles: docs + javadoc + maven + Mars.json.
_site/
# The Mars.json that workflow downloads from the already-published site to
# check that it really resolves.
published.json

# Packages produced by scripts/package-release.mjs: build artifacts that live
# in the GitHub releases, not in the repository.
release/

# Ares: PathPlanner and Choreo cloned for study, not part of this repository.
# They keep their own licenses (MIT and BSD-3); see ares/README.md.
ares/reference/
